    {
      "kind": "ability",
      "name": "Expert Subsistence",
      "category": "interaction",
      "text": "While using Survival to subsist statistic=survival, if the tracker rolls any result worse than a success, they get a success. On a success, they can provide subsistence living for themselves and 8 additional creatures, and on a critical success, they can take care of twice as many creatures as on a success.",
      "rules": [
        {
          "key": "degree",
          "selector": "survival",
          "adjust": {
            "critical-failure": "to-success",
            "failure": "to-success"
          },
          "when": [
            "action:subsist"
          ]
        },
        {
          "key": "note",
          "selector": "survival",
          "text": "{item|system.description.value}",
          "outcome": [
            "criticalSuccess",
            "success"
          ],
          "when": [
            "action:subsist"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "ability",
      "name": "Master Tracker",
      "category": "interaction",
      "text": "The tracker can Track while moving at full speed."
    },
    {
      "kind": "ability",
      "name": "On the Hunt",
      "actions": 1,
      "category": "offensive",
      "traits": [
        "concentrate"
      ],
      "text": "The tracker designates one creature they're observing or tracking as their prey.\n\nThe tracker gains a +2 circumstance bonus to Perception checks to seek the prey and to Survival checks to track the prey.\n\nThe first time the tracker hits the designated prey in a round, they deal an additional 1d4 precision damage. These effects last until the tracker uses On the Hunt again.",
      "rules": [
        {
          "key": "roll-option",
          "option": "hunted-prey",
          "toggleable": true,
          "label": "PF2E.SpecificRule.HuntPrey.TargetHuntedPrey"
        },
        {
          "key": "modifier",
          "selector": "perception",
          "type": "circumstance",
          "value": 2,
          "when": [
            "action:seek",
            "hunted-prey"
          ]
        },
        {
          "key": "modifier",
          "selector": "survival",
          "type": "circumstance",
          "value": 2,
          "when": [
            "action:track",
            "hunted-prey"
          ]
        },
        {
          "key": "roll-option",
          "option": "ignore-range-penalty:2",
          "domain": "ranged-attack-roll",
          "when": [
            "hunted-prey"
          ]
        },
        {
          "key": "roll-option",
          "option": "first-attack",
          "toggleable": true,
          "label": "PF2E.SpecificRule.Ranger.HuntersEdge.FirstAttack"
        },
        {
          "key": "damage-dice",
          "selector": "strike-damage",
          "dice": 1,
          "die": "d4",
          "category": "precision",
          "when": [
            "first-attack"
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "text": "An untrained eye might spot a sign or two of a wild creature's passing, but only a skilled tracker can identify several such signs and discern their relationship to each other, connecting one to the next until they form a trail of prints, scat, fur, feathers, and blood that leads to the quarry's lair.\n\n---\nExplorers are often well-equipped and well-trained for any type of hazard and are eager to lead others into the wild."
